<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eitel Frederick IV, Count of Hohenzollern-Hechingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1545">1545</a>–<a href="/years/1605">1605</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eitel Frederick IV was the first Count of Hohenzollern-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hechingen">Hechingen</a>, receiving the ancestral Hohenzollern castle and the town of Hechingen in the 1576 division of the County of Hohenzollern among the sons of Charles I. A patron of music and building, he made Hechingen a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> court. His line later became princes and ruled until 1849.</p></div>
